       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. DA5TSORTKEY.
      *> DA5 - A TABLE-SORT KEY THAT IS A GROUP CONTAINING A BINARY
      *> LEAF. V59 GAVE SUCH A LEAF ITS PINNED BYTE IMAGE AND
      *> RecordStructEmitter EMITS THE GROUP'S AsImage() FOR EXACTLY
      *> THAT PREDICATE (IsImageCapable), BUT SortEmitter WAS LEFT ON
      *> THE PRE-V59 IsCharacterImage AND THREW "NO WHOLE-GROUP
      *> CHARACTER IMAGE" - A CLAIM V59 FALSIFIED.
      *>
      *> ⛔ THE LOAD-BEARING RULE: 14.9.40.4 GR8 - KEY DATA ITEMS ARE
      *> "COMPARED ACCORDING TO THE RULES FOR COMPARISON OF OPERANDS
      *> IN A RELATION CONDITION". A GROUP OPERAND IN A RELATION IS
      *> CLASS ALPHANUMERIC (8.8.4.2.3 SR2) COMPARED OVER ITS
      *> REPRESENTATION, WHICH OperandText ALREADY RENDERS THROUGH
      *> AsImage() GATED ON IsImageCapable. SO SORT AND *IF* MUST GIVE
      *> THE SAME ANSWER FOR THE SAME TWO GROUP OPERANDS. BEFORE THE
      *> FIX THEY DID NOT: THE IF COMPARED THE BYTE IMAGES WHILE THE
      *> SORT THREW. THIS GOLDEN PINS THE *AGREEMENT*, NOT MERELY THAT
      *> THE SORT RUNS - AGREEMENT IS THE ACTUAL REQUIREMENT.
      *>
      *> ⚠ AND IT PINS A CONSEQUENCE THAT IS DELIBERATE, NOT A BUG:
      *> A BIG-ENDIAN TWO'S-COMPLEMENT IMAGE IS NOT ORDER-PRESERVING
      *> ACROSS ZERO, SO A GROUP KEY HOLDING -1 (BYTES FF FF) SORTS
      *> *AFTER* ONE HOLDING +1 (BYTES 00 01). THAT IS WHAT THE
      *> STANDARD PRESCRIBES FOR A *GROUP* KEY, AND THE IF AGREES. A
      *> PROGRAM WANTING VALUE ORDER NAMES THE ELEMENTARY NUMERIC ITEM
      *> AS THE KEY, WHICH COMPARES BY VALUE INSTEAD. WITHOUT THIS
      *> CASE A LATER READER WOULD "FIX" THE BYTE ORDER AND BREAK GR8.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 T.
          05 E OCCURS 3 TIMES ASCENDING KEY IS K INDEXED BY IX.
             10 K.
                15 KN PIC S9(4) COMP.
                15 KA PIC X(2).
             10 PAY PIC X(3).
       01 S.
          05 F OCCURS 2 TIMES ASCENDING KEY IS FK INDEXED BY JX.
             10 FK.
                15 FN PIC S9(4) COMP.
                15 FA PIC X(2).
             10 FPAY PIC X(3).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
      *> ALL-POSITIVE KEYS: BYTE ORDER AND VALUE ORDER COINCIDE.
           MOVE 300 TO KN(1).
           MOVE "cc" TO KA(1).
           MOVE "ccc" TO PAY(1).
           MOVE 100 TO KN(2).
           MOVE "aa" TO KA(2).
           MOVE "aaa" TO PAY(2).
           MOVE 200 TO KN(3).
           MOVE "bb" TO KA(3).
           MOVE "bbb" TO PAY(3).
           SORT E ON ASCENDING KEY K.
           DISPLAY "POS 1=" PAY(1) " 2=" PAY(2) " 3=" PAY(3).
      *> A NEGATIVE KEY: THE IF AND THE SORT MUST STILL AGREE.
           MOVE -1 TO FN(1).
           MOVE "nn" TO FA(1).
           MOVE "NEG" TO FPAY(1).
           MOVE 1 TO FN(2).
           MOVE "pp" TO FA(2).
           MOVE "POS" TO FPAY(2).
           IF FK(1) > FK(2)
               DISPLAY "IF  NEG-GT-POS"
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "IF  NEG-LT-POS"
           END-IF.
           SORT F ON ASCENDING KEY FK.
           DISPLAY "SRT 1=" FPAY(1) " 2=" FPAY(2).
           STOP RUN.
